COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[396,"§Al-Qasas, Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nCall others to Allah in the best way you know how.\nSupplicate Allah, saying: \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion\", because the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say that often.\nRead about some of the Prophet's Companions who were subjected to trial, like: Salman Al-Farsi, or Ammar bin Yasir, and how they endured truthfully and patiently.\nguid\nBad companions are harmful and a reason for turning away from the way of Allah.\nThe servant must fear from shirk. If Allah prohibited His Prophet (ﷺ) from invoking other than Him, then it is even more so for those who are below him.\nStriving is a great virtue, as it saves the soul.\nrefl\nوَلَا يَصُدُّنَّكَ عَنۡ ءَايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ بَعۡدَ إِذۡ أُنزِلَتۡ إِلَيۡكَۖ وَٱدۡعُ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَۖ وَلَا تَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٨٧\nMeaning: Never let them avert you by their words, lies, and annoyances, pay no heed to them, and go about your affair. Al-Qurtubi: 16/330.\nThis verse encourages preaching despite daunting difficulties. How?\nأَحَسِبَ ٱلنَّاسُ أَن يُتۡرَكُوٓاْ أَن يَقُولُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا وَهُمۡ لَا يُفۡتَنُونَ ٢\nDo people think they will be left without being tested or afflicted? (Once they say), just by uttering: (\"We believe,\" and they will not be tried), that they will not be tested in their wealth and themselves. No, We will try them to differentiate the sincere from the hypocrite, and the truthful from the liar. Al-Baghawi: 3/461.\nWhy does Allah try His servants?\nأَحَسِبَ ٱلنَّاسُ أَن يُتۡرَكُوٓاْ أَن يَقُولُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا وَهُمۡ لَا يُفۡتَنُونَ ٢\nThis verse was revealed because a group of believers in Makkah were persecuted by the disbelievers from Quraish. As a result, the believers became desperate, so Allah consoled them with this verse, admonished them, and told them that it was a trial in order to change this state of agitation into forbearance against adversity and be steadfast in faith. Allah informs the believers that this is His way with His servants; He empowers the disbelievers over the believers as a test for them in order to make evident who is truthful in his faith and who is a liar. This verse is general in its words and meanings, therefore, it applies to everyone who is afflicted by a trial due to a sin, or has been harmed in himself, his wealth, and akin to that. Ibn Juzay: 2/154.\nGiven this verse, explain the benefits of trials.\nوَلَقَدۡ فَتَنَّا ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۖ فَلَيَعۡلَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ صَدَقُواْ وَلَيَعۡلَمَنَّ ٱلۡكَٰذِبِينَ ٣\n(Those before them), the believing followers of the Prophets (p). They were afflicted with all sorts of trials and adversities, but they endured patiently, and clung to their religion stubbornly, literally: with their molar teeth, as Allah says, (How many prophets along with the devout men fought, but they did not lose heart because of what they suffered in the way of Allah, nor did they weaken or submit) [3:146]. Al-Alusi: 10/340.\nOne of the ways of Allah is trying the believers. What must the believer do in this case?\nوَلَقَدۡ فَتَنَّا ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۖ فَلَيَعۡلَمَنَّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ صَدَقُواْ وَلَيَعۡلَمَنَّ ٱلۡكَٰذِبِينَ ٣\nAllah certainly knows about them before the trial, but to make evident those who are truthful and those who are liars, so that the eternal knowledge of Allah about them will manifest. Al-Baghawi: 3/462.\nSince Allah knows everything, what is meant by (Allah will surely make known)?\nأَمۡ حَسِبَ ٱلَّذِينَ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٱلسَّيِّـَٔاتِ أَن يَسۡبِقُونَاۚ\nDo those whose main concern is doing evil deeds and committing sins think that their deeds will be ignored, and that Allah will be heedless to them, or that they can escape Him, and that is why they did those deeds, and it was easy for them to do so. Al-Saadi: 626.\nWhat makes committing sins easier for the servant?\nمَن كَانَ يَرۡجُواْ لِقَآءَ ٱللَّهِ فَإِنَّ أَجَلَ ٱللَّهِ لَأٓتٖۚ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٥\nMeaning of the verse: Whoever hopes for Allah's reward, let him strive patiently in obeying Allah until he meets and is rewarded by Him, as the time appointed by Allah is soon to come. Ibn Juzay: 2/155.\nWhat is required to receive Allah's reward?\nwords\nفَرَضَHe revealed\nلَرَآدُّكَ إِلَى مَعَادٍHe will take you back to the place you left, Makkah\nتَرجُوYou expect\nيُلقَىIt is revealed\nظَهِيرًاSupporter\nأَن يَسبِقُونَاThey escape Us"],[397,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nDo good to your parents by buying a gift for them.\nRead a book about the knowledge of trials.\nAdvise a collogue of yours not to send a prohibited message by mobile phone, lest he would bear the sin of everyone who is influenced by it, or resending it to others.\nguid\nIt is a duty to maintain kindness to parents in what is lawful and disobey them in what is unlawful, like shirk and sins.\nIf you find yourself in a sin, beware of inviting others to do the same, lest you would bear the sin of everyone who joins in doing it.\nIt is important to follow the example of the Prophets (p) in their patience and effort in calling to Allah.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَنُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنۡهُمۡ سَئِّاتِهِمۡ وَلَنَجۡزِيَنَّهُمۡ أَحۡسَنَ ٱلَّذِي كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٧\nMeaning: Their reward will be based on the best of their deeds, which is obedience. It is also said: We will give them more and much better than they did. Al-Baghawi: 3/463.\nAllah will reward the believers according to the best of what they used to do. How?\nوَإِن جَٰهَدَاكَ لِتُشۡرِكَ بِي مَا لَيۡسَ لَكَ بِهِۦ عِلۡمٞ فَلَا تُطِعۡهُمَآۚ إِلَيَّ مَرۡجِعُكُمۡ فَأُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٨ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَنُدۡخِلَنَّهُمۡ فِي ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ٩\nWhen the believer is commanded to disobey his parents if they enjoined him to associate partners with Allah, this would lead to estrangement between him and his parents, therefore, Allah made the pleasure of being among the righteous as a reward for that estrangement. Ibn Ashur: 20/215.\nAllah will greatly reward those who put his obedience before that of others. Explain.\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَقُولُ ءَامَنَّا بِٱللَّهِ فَإِذَآ أُوذِيَ فِي ٱللَّهِ جَعَلَ فِتۡنَةَ ٱلنَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ ٱللَّهِۖ\nMeaning: He considers the torture by the people as if it were the punishment of Allah in the Hereafter, which means that he becomes desperate and loses his patience against the torture by the people, thus, he will obey the people just like someone who obeys Allah out of fear of His punishment. Al-Baghawi: 3/464.\nThe hypocrite makes the persecution by the people as if it were Allah’s punishment. How?\nوَلَيَحۡمِلُنَّ أَثۡقَالَهُمۡ وَأَثۡقَالٗا مَّعَ أَثۡقَالِهِمۡۖ\nHere, Allah makes clear that those who call others to disbelief and misguidance will, on the Day of Resurrection, bear their own sins and the sins of others, because of the people they misguided. Yet that will not detract from the burden of those other people in the slightest. Ibn Kathir: 6/226.\nIs the sin of one who calls others to evil the same as theirs? Explain in view of the verse.\nوَلَيَحۡمِلُنَّ أَثۡقَالَهُمۡ وَأَثۡقَالٗا مَّعَ أَثۡقَالِهِمۡۖ\nFor each sin committed by the follower, both the follower and the one whom he followed will have a share of it, the follower because he himself did it and the one whom he followed because he was the cause of his doing it and he called him to do it. By the same token, if the follower does a good deed, he will have the reward for doing it himself, and the one who called him to it will have a reward for being the cause of it. Al-Saadi: 627.\nThis verse implicitly urges the believers to call others to Allah. Explain.\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦ فَلَبِثَ فِيهِمۡ أَلۡفَ سَنَةٍ إِلَّا خَمۡسِينَ عَامٗا فَأَخَذَهُمُ ٱلطُّوفَانُ وَهُمۡ ظَٰلِمُونَ ١٤\nIn the Arabic text, two different words for the word (year) are used in this verse: Sanah and A'am. So, the original verse reads: (for a thousand sanah, less fifty a'am). The word \"Sanah\" is normally used to describe a period of hardship and drought, which is unlike \"A'am.\" The choice of the word \"Sanah\" is suitable to reflect the hardship that Noah (u) suffered from his people while preaching them. Al-Alusi: 10/348.\nIn the original Arabic text, the word \"Sanah\" is used for (year). Why?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا نُوحًا إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِۦ فَلَبِثَ فِيهِمۡ أَلۡفَ سَنَةٍ إِلَّا خَمۡسِينَ عَامٗا فَأَخَذَهُمُ ٱلطُّوفَانُ وَهُمۡ ظَٰلِمُونَ ١٤\nSo, O Muhammad, do not feel sorry because of those among your people who disbelieve in you, and do not grieve over them, for Allah guides whomsoever He wills and leaves astray whomsoever He wills. The matter rests with Him and all things will return to Him. Ibn Kathir: 3/393.\nCan the human mind attain guidance on its own? How can guidance be attained?\nwords\nفِتنَةَ النَّاسِPersecution by people\nسَبِيلَنَاOur religion\nأَثقَالَهُمSins\nيَفتَرُونَThey fabricate lies"],[398,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to give you provision, then strive to pursue the means for it.\nRead some Prophetic Hadiths from the section on \"The beginning of creation\" from Sahih Al-Bukhari, to reflect on Allah's great power.\nWatch a documentary or pictures about the stages of human embryonic development to remind you of your beginning.\nguid\nOnly Allah is Capable of ending poverty and providing provision while everyone besides Him is helpless, so, we must invoke Him directly.\nThis is an affirmation of man's complete helplessness, and that he has nowhere to escape to, except through his faith and fear of Allah.\nDespairing of Allah's mercy is one of the reasons for punishment and destruction.\nrefl\nفَأَنجَيۡنَٰهُ وَأَصۡحَٰبَ ٱلسَّفِينَةِ وَجَعَلۡنَٰهَآ ءَايَةٗ لِّلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ١٥\n(A sign for all people), since those who did not see Noah's Ark can see the ships and envision the Ark, and how it was constructed by inspiration from Allah to save Noah (u) and whomever Allah wills. Moreover, those who were close to this event talked about it, and its news has become spread through the times and places. Ibn Ashur: 20/223.\nHow did Noah's Ark become a sign for all people?\nإِنَّمَا تَعۡبُدُونَ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡثَٰنٗا وَتَخۡلُقُونَ إِفۡكًاۚ\nAbraham (u) said: (idols), which indicates attentional dispersion due to multiple gods; multiplicity leads to division, and no good can come out of it. Al-Biqai: 14/407.\nIn this verse, the word, (idols) is plural. Why?\nفَٱبۡتَغُواْ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرِّزۡقَ وَٱعۡبُدُوهُ وَٱشۡكُرُواْ لَهُۥٓۖ إِلَيۡهِ تُرۡجَعُونَ ١٧\n(So seek): Indicates exerting an effort, since Allah's way is providing provision to those who make the effort to attain it. The effort can be through worship and reliance on Allah, or by the apparent pursuit of adopting its worldly means to attain it, but the helpless is the one who follows his own whims, and then indulges in wishful thinking about Allah. Al-Biqai: 14/412-413.\nThe verse points to the fact that attaining provision requires pursuing its means. How?\nقُلۡ سِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَٱنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ بَدَأَ ٱلۡخَلۡقَۚ ثُمَّ ٱللَّهُ يُنشِئُ ٱلنَّشۡأَةَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ٢٠\n(And observe how He began creation), observe their great multitude, different images, and the diversity of their tongues, colors, and qualities. Reflect on the dwellings of previous nations, their ruins, what they left behind, and how Allah destroyed them, so you will know His perfect power. Al-Qurtubi: 17/352.\nMention three examples of Allah's power.\nيُعَذِّبُ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَرۡحَمُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَإِلَيۡهِ تُقۡلَبُونَ ٢١\nMeaning: You will be returned to that realm where you will be subjected to punishment or mercy, so seek in this realm that which will be the cause of His mercy, by doing acts of obedience, and keep away from that which will be the cause of His wrath, namely acts of disobedience. Al-Saadi: 629.\nHow does the Muslim benefit from knowing that the final return will be to Allah?\nيُعَذِّبُ مَن يَشَآءُ وَيَرۡحَمُ مَن يَشَآءُۖ وَإِلَيۡهِ تُقۡلَبُونَ ٢١\nPunishment is mentioned first because it addresses those who deny the resurrection, and their share will be punishment. Ibn Ashur: 20/232.\nPunishment is mentioned first in this verse. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ وَلِقَآئِهِۦٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ يَئِسُواْ مِن رَّحۡمَتِي وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ٢٣\nThe disbelievers' despair has two possibilities: Either it will be in the Hereafter, or it describes their situation in this worldly life, since the disbeliever does not hope for Allah's mercy, but the believer combines both, hope in Allah's mercy, and fear of His punishment. Ibn Juzay: 2/157.\nWhat is the difference between how the believer and the disbeliever view Allah's mercy?\nwords\nوَتَخلُقُونَ إِفكًاYou fabricate lies\nفَابتَغُواSeek and request\nبَدَأَ الخَلقَHe began creation\nتُقلَبُونَYou will be returned\nبِمُعجِزِينَEscape His punishment"],[399,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nSay, \"Allah is Sufficient for me, and He is the best Disposer of affairs,\" as it is a way out of adversities, and Abraham (u) said it when he was thrown into the fire.\nAbandoning a sin that you know from yourself, or a companion who invites you to do wrong, is a form of migration to Allah.\nForbid wrongdoing that you have seen through exhortation and logical persuasion.\nguid\nA true believer is confident of Allah's defense and help for those who stand up for His religion.\nWhen wrongdoers are defeated by proof, they resort to using force.\nWhoever gives up something for the sake of Allah, Allah will give him something much better instead, in this world and in the Hereafter.\nrefl\nفَمَا كَانَ جَوَابَ قَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِلَّآ أَن قَالُواْ ٱقۡتُلُوهُ أَوۡ حَرِّقُوهُ\nThis was because proof had clearly been established against them, so they resorted to using their power and strength. Ibn Kathir: 3/395.\nWhat does it indicate when wrongdoers resort to using power?\nفَأَنجَىٰهُ ٱللَّهُ مِنَ ٱلنَّارِۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٢٤\nThere are signs, not one, in saving Abraham (u) from the fire, since it was a sign for all those who witnessed it, a sign of Allah's capability, a sign of His Messenger's honor, a sign of fulfilling Allah's promise, a sign of His enemy's abasement, and a manifestation of Allah's power over all created beings, big and small. Ibn Ashur: 20/235.\nThere are signs, not one, in saving Abraham (u) from the fire. Explain.\nوَقَالَ إِنَّمَا ٱتَّخَذۡتُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡثَٰنٗا مَّوَدَّةَ بَيۡنِكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ ثُمَّ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ يَكۡفُرُ بَعۡضُكُم بِبَعۡضٖ وَيَلۡعَنُ بَعۡضُكُم بَعۡضٗا\nThis includes anyone who joins his disobedient friends in evildoing, in order to seek their approval and be considered a nice and easy-going friend, or to avoid being described as an unpleasant and disagreeable person. Unfortunately, this attitude has become very common among people these days aiming to be viewed as loyal and sincere friends, while turning away from what pleases Allah, the King, the Judge. Al-Biqai: 14/424.\nThere are limits to pleasing friends and companions. Explain in view of this verse.\nوَقَالَ إِنَّمَا ٱتَّخَذۡتُم مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡثَٰنٗا مَّوَدَّةَ بَيۡنِكُمۡ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَاۖ ثُمَّ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ يَكۡفُرُ بَعۡضُكُم بِبَعۡضٖ وَيَلۡعَنُ بَعۡضُكُم بَعۡضٗا\nQatadah said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, close friends will become enemies to one another, except the righteous.\" Al-Tabari: 20/25.\nExplain the benefit of a righteous friendship and the consequence of an evil one.\nثُمَّ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡقِيَٰمَةِ يَكۡفُرُ بَعۡضُكُم بِبَعۡضٖ وَيَلۡعَنُ بَعۡضُكُم بَعۡضٗا\nThe idols will disown their worshipers, the leaders will disown their followers, and the followers will curse their leaders. Al-Baghawi: 3/467.\nWhat will be the consequences, on the Day of Resurrection, of following others in disobeying Allah?\n۞فَـَٔامَنَ لَهُۥ لُوطٞۘ وَقَالَ إِنِّي مُهَاجِرٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّيٓۖ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٢٦\nAllah does not mention that He destroyed them with any punishment; rather He states that Abraham left them and migrated elsewhere. If Allah had eradicated them all through punishment, He would have mentioned that as He mentioned the destruction of other disbelieving nations. Perhaps the reason why they were not destroyed is that Abraham, who was one of the most compassionate, virtuous, forbearing, and noble of all people, did not pray against his people as others did. What may indicate that is the fact that he disputed and argued with the angels concerning the destruction of Lot's people, and tried to defend them, although they were not his people. And Allah knows best what really happened. Al-Saadi: 629-630.\nAmong the traits of the allies of Allah is that they are most compassionate toward others. Explain in light of Abraham’s (u) story.\nوَلُوطًا إِذۡ قَالَ لِقَوۡمِهِۦٓ إِنَّكُمۡ لَتَأۡتُونَ ٱلۡفَٰحِشَةَ مَا سَبَقَكُم بِهَا مِنۡ أَحَدٖ مِّنَ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢٨\nPeople are oblivious to many criminal acts because they are not accustomed to them until someone commits them and they become known, alerting people's minds to them, thus, their desires become attached to them. Ibn Ashur: 20/241.\nExplain the risk of setting a bad example in committing sins.\nwords\nمَوَدَّةَ بَينِكُمAs a bond of affection among you\nيَكفُرُDisowns\nوَمَأوَاكُمُYour destination\nمُهَاجِرٌEmigrating from my land to the Levant\nأَجرَهُ فِي الدُّنيَاHe is rewarded in this world with a good prominence, righteous offspring, and prophethood in his descendants\nنَادِيكُمُYour gatherings"],[400,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nLearn about the righteous people around you, become aware of what they are going through, and protect them.\nHelp a friend of yours by relieving the distress he is going through.\nSay, \"O Allah, do not take us into account for what the fools among us have done.\"\nguid\nFaith and good deeds protect one from punishment. Being married to a person with these characteristics without having them yourself will not benefit you in any way.\nReminding yourself about the Hereafter and fearing its terror, is one of the most effective ways to abandon sins.\nOne of the devil's steps to misguide people into committing sins is by making their deeds appealing to them, so, be extremely cautious of that.\nrefl\nوَلَمَّا جَآءَتۡ رُسُلُنَآ إِبۡرَٰهِيمَ بِٱلۡبُشۡرَىٰ قَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا مُهۡلِكُوٓاْ أَهۡلِ هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِۖ إِنَّ أَهۡلَهَا كَانُواْ ظَٰلِمِينَ ٣١\nOut of His grace, Allah gave glad tidings to Abraham (u) before informing him about the destruction of Lot’s people because He knew of Abraham's compassion. Ibn Ashur: 20/242.\nAllah gave glad tidings to Abraham before informing him about the destruction of Lot's people. Why?\nإِنَّا مُنزِلُونَ عَلَىٰٓ أَهۡلِ هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡقَرۡيَةِ رِجۡزٗا مِّنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَفۡسُقُونَ ٣٤\nIbn Abbas said: Lot's people had many sins other than the shameful act, such as: Transgressing and reviling one another, and transvestism in men and women was common. They exacted imposts on every passing traveler, they were polytheists, and they were the first, of all mankind, who committed sodomy and tribadism. Al-Qurtubi: 13/342.\nIn view of this verse, explain the reasons for the destruction of cities and nations.\nوَلَقَد تَّرَكۡنَا مِنۡهَآ ءَايَةَۢ بَيِّنَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٣٥\nMeaning: After We destroyed them, We left a (sign) showing what We did to them as a lesson and admonishment for (a people who use reason) in understanding the proofs from Allah, and reflect on His lessons. Al-Tabari: 20/33.\nWhat is the benefit of having the ruins of ancient generations still remaining?\nوَلَا تَعۡثَوۡاْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مُفۡسِدِينَ ٣٦\nMeaning: Do not disbelieve, since it is the origin of every corruption. Al-Qurtubi: 13/361.\nShu'ayb (u) forbade them from spreading corruption. What was it?\nوَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَصَدَّهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَكَانُواْ مُسۡتَبۡصِرِينَ ٣٨\n(And satan made their deeds appealing to them), through his whispering and temptation, satan made their evil deeds, like disbelief and sins, appealing to them. (They were people of perception), they were sane and able to differentiate between truth and falsehood through inference and thinking, but they neglected, and did not reflect. Al-Alusi: 10/362.\nWhat are the main ways of satan to misguide sane people?\nوَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَصَدَّهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَكَانُواْ مُسۡتَبۡصِرِينَ ٣٨\n(They were people of perception), they had insight about their disbelief and were drawn to it in admiration. Moreover, it is said that they had good awareness of faith and belief, but they disbelieved because of their stubbornness. Ibn Juzay: 2/159.\nIs ignorance the only reason for disbelief?\nوَزَيَّنَ لَهُمُ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ أَعۡمَٰلَهُمۡ فَصَدَّهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَكَانُواْ مُسۡتَبۡصِرِينَ ٣٨\n(They were people of perception), they recognized the truth from falsehood through clear proofs. Al-Farra said: \"They were sane and had perception, but it did not benefit them.\" Al-Qurtubi: 16/362.\nDoes a person's mind benefit him if he disobeys his Lord?\nwords\nبِالبُشرَىThe glad tidings of the birth of Isaac (u)\nالغَابِرِينَThose who remained in punishment\nوَضَاقَ بِهِم ذَرعًاHe was distressed and concerned for their safety\nرِجزًاA severe punishment\nوَلاَ تَعثَواDo not about spreading corruption\nالرَّجفَةُA powerful earthquake"],[401,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nSeek refuge with Allah from arrogance, for it is one of the reasons for rejecting the truth.\nRecite one of the surahs of the Quran, for it is the revelation that enlightens hearts, and sets right all worldly and religious affairs.\nPerform the five daily prayers in the best way, as it will prevent immoral deeds of the heart like, love and fear of other than Allah, and keep you from evildoing.\nguid\nAllah's justice entails that He does not punish anyone except for what he has earned.\nRemember that Allah does not wrong people in the least, but it is the servant who wrongs himself with his sins.\nKnowledge is a virtue, since it enables people to benefit from examples presented by Allah.\nrefl\nمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡلِيَآءَ كَمَثَلِ ٱلۡعَنكَبُوتِ ٱتَّخَذَتۡ بَيۡتٗاۖ وَإِنَّ أَوۡهَنَ ٱلۡبُيُوتِ لَبَيۡتُ ٱلۡعَنكَبُوتِۚ لَوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤١\nAl-Farra said: This is an example presented by Allah for those who took for themselves gods besides Allah, which do not benefit nor harm them, just like the spider's home that does not protect it against hot or cold. It means that if the polytheists knew that worshiping idols is like taking a spider's home that does not avail them anything, and this was their example, they would have not worshiped them. Al-Qurtubi: 16/363.\nExplain the point of similarity between spider's home, and gravesites and shrines that are worshiped besides Allah.\nمَثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ مِن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ أَوۡلِيَآءَ كَمَثَلِ ٱلۡعَنكَبُوتِ ٱتَّخَذَتۡ بَيۡتٗاۖ وَإِنَّ أَوۡهَنَ ٱلۡبُيُوتِ لَبَيۡتُ ٱلۡعَنكَبُوتِۚ لَوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٤١\nThe polytheists resemble the spider in being deluded by what they made. Their allies resemble the spider's home in its uselessness at the time of need, and its elimination by the slightest movement. Ibn Ashur: 20/252.\nWhat is the point of similarity between the polytheists and their allies, and the spider and its home?\nوَتِلۡكَ ٱلۡأَمۡثَٰلُ نَضۡرِبُهَا لِلنَّاسِۖ وَمَا يَعۡقِلُهَآ إِلَّا ٱلۡعَٰلِمُونَ ٤٣\nThese examples will be comprehended by those who have prudence, and thus become knowledgeable and wise. This alludes to the fact that those who did not benefit from them are ignorant, let alone those who mocked them instead of reflecting on their meanings. Ibn Ashur: 20/252.\nWhat is the risk of not reflecting on the examples of the Quran?\nوَتِلۡكَ ٱلۡأَمۡثَٰلُ نَضۡرِبُهَا لِلنَّاسِۖ وَمَا يَعۡقِلُهَآ إِلَّا ٱلۡعَٰلِمُونَ ٤٣\nThe reason for that is that the comparisons that Allah gives in the Quran have to do with important issues, sublime goals and noble ideas. Therefore, the people of knowledge understand that they are more important than others, because Allah mentions them and urges His slaves to reflect on them and ponder their meanings, and do their utmost to understand them. Al-Saadi: 631.\nThose who understand are singled out for knowing the examples. Why?\nٱتۡلُ مَآ أُوحِيَ إِلَيۡكَ مِنَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ وَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَۖ\nReciting the Quran often increases its understanding, and reveals the wealth of its subtle knowledge. By no means the Quran will reveal its benefits, and lift the veil off its unique jewels for a first-time reader. Rather, every time a reader reflects on it, it bestows upon him a bounty of its secrets. No matter how much the reader/reflector receives from its enlightenments, he will always affirm that its wonders are countless, and its rarities are limitless. Al-Biqai: 14/447.\nWhen does the Muslim benefit from reciting the Quran?\nوَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَۖ إِنَّ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ تَنۡهَىٰ عَنِ ٱلۡفَحۡشَآءِ وَٱلۡمُنكَرِۗ\nIt is narrated about one of the righteous predecessors; whenever he stood up for prayer, he became shivered and paled, so he was asked about that, and said: If I am standing before a king from this world, I should feel this way, let alone standing before Allah, the Almighty, the King of all kings. This is a definite prayer that restrains one from immoral acts and wickedness. When one whose prayer is based on dull movements without remembrance or humbleness, -like ours, and we wish it suffices- then it will leave him wherever he is. Al-Qurtubi: 16/367.\nWhat kind of prayer that restrains one from immoral acts and wickedness?\nوَأَقِمِ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَۖ إِنَّ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ تَنۡهَىٰ عَنِ ٱلۡفَحۡشَآءِ وَٱلۡمُنكَرِۗ\nWhen one humbly performs his prayer, remembering Allah's greatness, this will lead him to repent from immoral acts and wickedness, thus, his prayer restrained him from that. Ibn Juzay: 2/160.\nHow does the prayer restrain one from immoral acts and wickedness?\nwords\nوَمَا كَانُوا سَابِقِينَThey could not escape Allah's punishment\nأَخَذنَا بِذَنبِهِEach of them We seized for their sin\nحَاصِبًاA storm of stones\nأَوهَنَWeaker\nوَمَا يَعقِلُهَاReflect and understand"],[402,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nMemorize verses from the Quran today that you did not memorize before.\nPractice dialog, as it is one of the ways of the Prophets. Select a peer and dialog with him calmly and wisely, and make sure to be fair and just in your words.\nSupplicate Allah, the Almighty, to make you submissive to His command and law.\nguid\nA scholar is the one who knows the correct way of worship, even if he does not read or write.\nThe Quran is at the highest level of eloquence, even though it was conveyed by our illiterate Prophet (ﷺ) who could neither read nor write .\nRevealing the Best Book to the best Messenger is Allah's bounty on this Muslim Ummah.\nrefl\n۞وَلَا تُجَٰدِلُوٓاْ أَهۡلَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ إِلَّا بِٱلَّتِي هِيَ أَحۡسَنُ إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ظَلَمُواْ مِنۡهُمۡۖ وَقُولُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا بِٱلَّذِيٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡنَا وَأُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكُمۡ وَإِلَٰهُنَا وَإِلَٰهُكُمۡ وَٰحِدٞ وَنَحۡنُ لَهُۥ مُسۡلِمُونَ ٤٦\nThe instruction to conduct a discussion with the people of the Scripture in the best manner is because they believe in Allah, and are not polytheists; therefore, they are less likely to be contentious and more likely to accept the arguments. Moreover, the teachings of their religion and Scripture prepared them for discussion and reasoning, therefore, arguing with them should be limited to clearly stating the proofs without displaying harshness, lest they be turned off. Ibn Ashur: 21/6.\nWe are instructed to argue with the people of the Scripture in the best manner. Why?\nوَقُولُوٓاْ ءَامَنَّا بِٱلَّذِيٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡنَا وَأُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكُمۡ وَإِلَٰهُنَا وَإِلَٰهُكُمۡ وَٰحِدٞ\nMeaning: Do not frame your argument with them in a way that it leads to you criticizing any of the divinely-revealed Books or any of the Messengers, as the ignorant do when arguing and criticizing everything that they have, whether it is right or wrong. This is unfair and is drifting away from the proper manners and etiquette of debate. What one should do is reject what one's opponent has of falsehood and accept what he has of truth, and not reject the truth just because he said it, even if he is a disbeliever. Al-Saadi: 632.\nArguing with disbelievers is based on fairness and prudence. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَنزَلۡنَآ إِلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَۚ فَٱلَّذِينَ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِهِۦۖ وَمِنۡ هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ مَن يُؤۡمِنُ بِهِۦۚ وَمَا يَجۡحَدُ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ إِلَّا ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٤٧\nThe verb (believe) is in the present tense to indicate its occurrence in the future, or the renewal of the belief by this group; that is, the number of those who believe increases every day. Ibn Ashur: 21/9.\nIn this verse, the verb (believe) is in the present tense. Why?\nوَمَا يَجۡحَدُ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ إِلَّا ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٤٧\nThose who persistently deny the truth and stubbornly reject it. This states that only the disbelievers reject Allah’s revelation since rejection cannot come from ones whose aim is to follow the truth. Otherwise, anyone with good intentions will inevitably believe in it, for what it contains of clear proofs for anyone who has sound reason or who pays heed.Al-Saadi: 633.\nDo those who have good intentions deny the Quran?\nبَلۡ هُوَ ءَايَٰتُۢ بَيِّنَٰتٞ فِي صُدُورِ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَۚ وَمَا يَجۡحَدُ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ إِلَّا ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَ ٤٩\nAlhasan said: \"This [Muslims] Ummah were given memorization, while those before them could recite only by looking in their Books, and once they closed them, they did not memorize anything except the Prophets.\" Al-Qurtubi: 16/376.\nMemorizing the Quran is a great virtue. Explain.\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَكۡفِهِمۡ أَنَّآ أَنزَلۡنَا عَلَيۡكَ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ يُتۡلَىٰ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَرَحۡمَةٗ وَذِكۡرَىٰ لِقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ٥١\nMeaning: How do they request a sign while the Holy Quran is the greatest of all signs, and the clearest proof of Prophethood. Should they not be content to have the Quran instead of requesting other signs. Ibn Juzay: 2/161.\nThe revelation of the Quran is a response to those who claim that the Prophet (ﷺ) came up with it. How?\nقُلۡ كَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَكُمۡ شَهِيدٗاۖ\nMeaning: Allah knows what I am telling you about Him, and that He has sent me. If I were telling lies about Him, He would have executed His vengeance upon me. Ibn Kathir: 3/404.\nAllah testifies to the truthfulness of Muhammad's (ﷺ) Prophethood. How?\nwords\nظَلَمُوا مِنهُمThose who reject the truth and declared war\nمُسلِمُونَSubmissive and humbled through obedience\nوَمِن هَؤُلاَءِFrom the Arabs in Makkah\nلَولاَWhy not\nآيَاتٌVisible signs, like Salih's (u) she camel"],[403,"§Al-Ankabut\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to give you patience, and help you endure it.\nDetermine the times you are able to work in your day and week, then divide them between working for this world and for the Hereafter, knowing that your provision depends on Allah, not your effort.\nLook at the ants and birds and how Allah gives them their provisions, then supplicate Allah to give you lawful, good, and blessed provision.\nguid\nBeware of encountering the end of your life while persisting on sins.\nThere is no excuse for anyone to abandon Allah's worship and His Oneness, because if he is prevented from doing so in one country, he must migrate to another.\nDo not be concerned about your provision, as Allah has taken care of it for you.\nrefl\nيَوۡمَ يَغۡشَىٰهُمُ ٱلۡعَذَابُ مِن فَوۡقِهِمۡ وَمِن تَحۡتِ أَرۡجُلِهِمۡ\nThe Fire will cover them from all sides, which is more effective as a physical punishment. Ibn Kathir: 3/404.\nThe punishment will cover them from above them and from below their feet. Why?\nوَيَقُولُ ذُوقُواْ مَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ٥٥\nThis is a form of an emotional punishment upon the souls. Ibn Kathir: 3/404.\nWhy it will be said to them: \"Taste [the punishment] for what you used to do\"?\nيَٰعِبَادِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّ أَرۡضِي وَٰسِعَةٞ فَإِيَّٰيَ فَٱعۡبُدُونِ ٥٦\nIf you are unable to worship your Lord in one land, then leave it and travel to another land where worship is for Allah alone, for places, where one may worship Allah, are vast and spacious, and the Lord is One. Al-Saadi: 634.\nWhat is the point of informing the believers that the earth is spacious?\nيَٰعِبَادِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّ أَرۡضِي وَٰسِعَةٞ فَإِيَّٰيَ فَٱعۡبُدُونِ ٥٦ كُلُّ نَفۡسٖ ذَآئِقَةُ ٱلۡمَوۡتِۖ ثُمَّ إِلَيۡنَا تُرۡجَعُونَ ٥٧\nDeath is mentioned here to disparage this worldly life, its gains and fears. Some believers may have thought that migrating from their homes in Makkah would result in their death, or that they would be stricken with hunger, among other things. Allah belittles worldly life and essentially says: Certainly, all of you will die and will be gathered before us; therefore, hasten to the obedience of Allah, migration to Him, and to what pleases Him. Al-Qurtubi: 16/382.\nWhat should be your response to one who says: How can I survive if I leave a land of disobedience in which is my provision?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَعَمِلُواْ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَنُبَوِّئَنَّهُم مِّنَ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ غُرَفٗا تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَاۚ نِعۡمَ أَجۡرُ ٱلۡعَٰمِلِينَ ٥٨\nAllah's promise and description of Paradise to the believers is also meant to console them, and minimize the adversities they face in the cause of Allah -even if it ends in death- in comparison to Allah's bounty and His eternal reward that awaits them in the Hereafter. Ibn Ashur: 21/23.\nIn light of this verse, explain the insignificance of adversities faced by the believer compared to the great reward that awaits him in the Hereafter.\nوَكَأَيِّن مِّن دَآبَّةٖ لَّا تَحۡمِلُ رِزۡقَهَا ٱللَّهُ يَرۡزُقُهَا وَإِيَّاكُمۡۚ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٦٠\nMeaning: How many a weak creature that does not carry its provision, but Allah provides for it. The aim of this verse is to strengthen the believers' hearts if they fear poverty and hunger when they migrate to other people’s land; that is, just like He provides provisions for weak animals, He will provide for you when you migrate from your homeland.Ibn Juzay: 2/162.\nThis verse strengthens the believers' hearts and purifies their souls. Explain.\nوَكَأَيِّن مِّن دَآبَّةٖ لَّا تَحۡمِلُ رِزۡقَهَا ٱللَّهُ يَرۡزُقُهَا وَإِيَّاكُمۡۚ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٦٠\n(It is Allah Who provides for them and for you), this equates one who is eager with another who relies on Allah for his provision, one who desires with another who is content, and a cunning person with a helpless one, lest a strong person is not deluded by thinking that he obtains his provision through his strength, nor the helpless thinks that he is deprived due to his weakness. Al-Qurtubi: 16/386.\nIs the provision for an avid person increased because of his avidness?\nwords\nأَجَلٌ مُسَمّىًThe decreed time for their punishment\nيَغشَاهُمُCovers them\nوَكَأَيِّن مِنHow many?\nفَأَنَّى يُؤفَكُونَHow are they turning away from belief!\nيَبسُطُHe extends\nوَيَقدِرُHe restricts"],[404,"§Al-Ankabut, Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nGive thanks to Allah for the blessings of safety and security.\nDo a deed that Allah loves, even if you find it hard.\nSpend something in the cause of Allah.\nguid\nThe blessing of security in homes and homelands is one of the greatest blessings, which is preserved by doing good deeds and honoring the symbols of Allah.\nThis is glad tidings from Allah for those who strive against the polytheists, and strive to guide themselves to His way.\nKnow that victory does not depend on the number of fighters or their equipment, but it is in the Hand of Allah, the Almighty, Who gives it to whomever He wills.\nrefl\nوَمَا هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ إِلَّا لَهۡوٞ وَلَعِبٞۚ\nThe demonstrative pronoun, (this), is used here to indicate the insignificance of worldly life. Ibn Ashur: 21/31.\nIn this verse, the demonstrative pronoun, (this), is used. Why?\nوَمَا هَٰذِهِ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَآ إِلَّا لَهۡوٞ وَلَعِبٞۚ وَإِنَّ ٱلدَّارَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَ لَهِيَ ٱلۡحَيَوَانُۚ لَوۡ كَانُواْ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٦٤\nMeaning: This worldly life is a play and distraction. There is nothing that is given to the wealthy in this life except that it will diminish and cease, like playing, which lacks reality and steadiness. Some scholars said: If worldly life stays with you, you will not stay with it. Al-Qurtubi: 16/387.\nExplain the reality of worldly life as it is described by its Creator, the Almighty.\nفَإِذَا رَكِبُواْ فِي ٱلۡفُلۡكِ دَعَوُاْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ فَلَمَّا نَجَّىٰهُمۡ إِلَى ٱلۡبَرِّ إِذَا هُمۡ يُشۡرِكُونَ ٦٥\nThey did not experience any fear when traveling through the desert, because they used to travel in caravans, with their arms, and the routes were well known to them, therefore, they never had fear in general. However, when they travel by sea, they become horrified at its turmoil that cannot be warded off by their number nor strength, hence, they invoke only Allah and none of their idols. Ibn Ashur: 21/32.\nTraveling by sea is singled out for experiencing fear. Why?\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ أَنَّا جَعَلۡنَا حَرَمًا ءَامِنٗا وَيُتَخَطَّفُ ٱلنَّاسُ مِنۡ حَوۡلِهِمۡۚ أَفَبِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ يُؤۡمِنُونَ وَبِنِعۡمَةِ ٱللَّهِ يَكۡفُرُونَ ٦٧\nMeaning: I made for them a safe sanctuary in which they felt safe from being captured, raided on, or being killed. I saved them while being on land as well as when at sea, yet, they associate partners with Me on land, but do not do that when at sea! This is a wander at their contradiction. Al-Qurtubi: 16/389.\nIn light of this verse, explain the polytheists’ contradiction.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ جَٰهَدُواْ فِينَا لَنَهۡدِيَنَّهُمۡ سُبُلَنَاۚ وَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَمَعَ ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٦٩\nAbu Sulayman Al-Darani said: The mentioned strive in this verse is not limited to Jihad against the disbelievers, but also supporting the religion, responding to falsifiers, suppressing wrongdoers, and most important of all, enjoining what is right and forbidding what is evil. Striving against oneself for the obedience of Allah is the greatest Jihad. Al-Qurtubi: 16/390.\nIs this great reward of guidance limited to fighting against the disbelievers only?\nلِلَّهِ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ مِن قَبۡلُ وَمِنۢ بَعۡدُۚ\nVictory does not occur just because of worldly means; rather it must also be according to the divine will and decree. Al-Saadi: 636.\nThis statement is mentioned in the story of Persia and the Romans. Why?\nوَيَوۡمَئِذٖ يَفۡرَحُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ ٤\nThe believers rejoiced at the victory of the Romans over Persia because the Romans were people of the Scripture, hence, they were closer to the religion of Islam. Similarly, the disbelievers of Quraish rejoiced at the victory of the Persians over the Romans because the Persians did not have a divine Scripture, and therefore, they were closer to the disbelievers of Quraish. Ibn Juzay: 2/164.\nThe believers rejoiced at the victory of the Romans even though the Romans were disbelievers. Why?\nwords\nالحَيَوَانُThe real complete eternal life\nالفُلكِShips\nوَيُتَخَطَّفُ النَّاسُPeople are snatched away, killed or captured\nمَثوىًHome, residence\nغُلِبَتِ الرُّومُPersia defeated the Romans\nأَدنَى الأَرضِNearest land to Persia, or in the lowest land\nبِضعِ سِنِينَA time period between three to ten years"],[405,"§Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nListen to a lecture on the description of Paradise and Hellfire.\nSelect one of your limbs, then reflect on how Allah created it, and write down three benefits you gained from your reflection.\nAsk Allah to grant you the intercession of the Prophet (ﷺ), and help you to follow his example.\nguid\nRelate what you learn from worldly sciences to Allah's greatness and Power so that you can benefit from them.\nReflection is one of the most important acts of worship, and whoever is blessed with it, is blessed with a vigilant heart, since it keeps him in constant contact with Allah.\nAffirming the belief that there will be no intercession for polytheists on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nوَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِۖ لَا يُخۡلِفُ ٱللَّهُ وَعۡدَهُۥ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٦\nAttributing the promise to Allah to signal its certain fulfillment, since the promise of the Truthful, the Able, the Self-sufficient can never be broken. Ibn Ashur: 21/48.\nWhat is the benefit of attributing the promise to Allah?\nيَعۡلَمُونَ ظَٰهِرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ غَٰفِلُونَ ٧\nIt is strange indeed that many of these types of people have a stunningly high level of smartness and intelligence with regard to superficial worldly matters. They have achieved amazing things in the fields of energy, electricity, and means of transportation on land, sea, and in the air. In that regard they have surpassed others. Yet despite of all that, they are the most unintelligent of people with regard to spiritual well-being, and they are more negligent than others with regard to the Hereafter, and have the least knowledge of the ultimate consequences of matters. When the people with deep insight saw them and learned how they are wandering blindly in ignorance, misguidance and falsehood; they realized that all matters are in the Hand of Allah and it is He Who decrees concerning His servants; it is He Who grants help and guidance, or causes some to fail. Hence, they fear their Lord and ask Him to perfect for them what He has granted them of the light of reason and faith, so that they may reach Him and draw close to Him. Al-Saadi: 637.\nHow do you maintain the balance between worldly sciences and religious knowledge?\nيَعۡلَمُونَ ظَٰهِرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ غَٰفِلُونَ ٧\nAlhasan said: \"One of them can determine the exact weight of a Dirham coin by flicking it with his finger, but he does not know how to perform prayer properly.\" The likes of this person are numerous, and while they may be praised by worldly people, they are, in fact, worthless in the sight of Allah, since they did not do more than making themselves comparable to animals that pursue what benefits them and evade what harms them through various tricks. Al-Biqai: 15/44-45.\nWhat type of knowledge that will be beneficial in the Hereafter?\nيَعۡلَمُونَ ظَٰهِرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ غَٰفِلُونَ ٧\nMeaning: They know how to handle their livelihood affairs; how to earn money and trade. They know when to sow the seeds, plant the trees, and harvest the crops. They know how to build and live, (but they are heedless of the Hereafter), oblivious and unwary of the Hereafter to such an extent that they do not think or work for it. Al-Baghawi: 3/488.\nWhen is it proper to censure those who are good in worldly knowledge?\nفَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيَظۡلِمَهُمۡ وَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٩\n(They who wronged themselves), they repeat wronging themselves by placing themselves in harm's way instead of pursuing their benefit, since they do not use the intellect that We gave them to enlighten their way and differentiate the truth from falsehood. They do not accept from guiding preachers when they remove the cover off their minds, nor will they back down from their way of error when the preachers overwhelm them with clear proofs; instead, they shift from heedlessness to stubbornness. Al-Biqai: 15/52.\nAbandoning the intellect is a form of wronging oneself. How?\nوَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٩\n(Wronging themselves), the continuous tense indicates the continuity and repetition of their wrongdoing, and that Allah gave them respite but they did not quit until He punished them. Ibn Ashur: 21/58.\n(Wronging themselves) is in the continuous tense. What does that indicate?\nوَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٩\n(Rejoicing), The state of bliss appears on them. (They will be rejoicing in a garden of Paradise), Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: It means listening to the sounds of Paradise. Al-Awza'i said the same when he said: \"When the people of Paradise take a listen, every tree therein will echo the glorification and exaltation of [Allah].\" Al-Qurtubi: 16/406.\nIn light of this verse, how will the state of believers be in Paradise?\nwords\nوَأَجَلٍ مُسَمّىًAn appointed term\nوَأَثَارُواThey tilled and planted the land\nالسُّوأَىThe worst punishment\nيُبلِسُDespairs of being saved from punishment\nيُحبَرُونَThey will be honored and granted eternal bliss"],[406,"§Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nSay, \"Glory and Praise be to Allah\" a hundred times in the evening, morning, afternoon, or at noon.\nStart memorizing what you did not memorize of the morning and evening Athkar (daily remembrance of Allah).\nHelp your parents in giving each other a gift as a token of affection and love.\nguid\nReward and punishment are among the fundamentals of discipline.\nRemembrance of Allah should be throughout the day.\nGlory be to Him who recognizes voices in different tongues, fulfills the needs, and forgives the slips.\nrefl\nيُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡحَيَّ مِنَ ٱلۡمَيِّتِ وَيُخۡرِجُ ٱلۡمَيِّتَ مِنَ ٱلۡحَيِّ\nAllah mentions the creation of things and their opposites to indicate to His creation the perfection of His power. Thus, He creates the plant from the seed and the seed from the plant; He creates the egg from the chicken and the chicken from the egg; He creates man from sperm and sperm from man; He creates the believer from the disbelievers, and the disbeliever from the believers. Ibn Kathir: 6/277.\nWhat is the benefit of knowing that Allah creates things and their opposites?\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦٓ أَنۡ خَلَقَ لَكُم مِّنۡ أَنفُسِكُمۡ أَزۡوَٰجٗا لِّتَسۡكُنُوٓاْ إِلَيۡهَا وَجَعَلَ بَيۡنَكُم مَّوَدَّةٗ وَرَحۡمَةًۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٢١\nAllah placed love and mercy between married couple; hence, they have affection and love for each other even though they are not related. (Indeed, there are signs in this for people who reflect) on Allah's greatness and power. Al-Baghawi: 3/491.\nDescribe Allah’s blessing in placing love and mercy between married couple.\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ خَلۡقُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱخۡتِلَٰفُ أَلۡسِنَتِكُمۡ وَأَلۡوَٰنِكُمۡۚ\nOne aspect of Allah's care and mercy toward His servants is that He has decreed these differences in tongues and colors, lest things resemble one another too closely, which would lead to confusion and would be detrimental to people’s interests. Al-Saadi: 639.\nA sign of Allah's mercy toward His servants is the diversity of tongues and colors. How?\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ خَلۡقُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱخۡتِلَٰفُ أَلۡسِنَتِكُمۡ وَأَلۡوَٰنِكُمۡۚ\nAll the people of this world, from the time that Allah created Adam, and until the Hour begins, each of them has two eyes, two eyebrows, a nose, a forehead, a mouth, and two cheeks but, none of them looks like another; there is bound to be some difference in posture, appearance, and speech, whether it is apparent or hidden, and can only be noticed with careful observation. Each face has its own characteristics and does not look like another; even if there was a group of people who looked alike, having a beautiful or ugly characteristic in common, there would still be a difference between one person and the next. Ibn Kathir: 6/279.\nWhen you reflect on the creation of people, what do we learn from that?\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ خَلۡقُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَٱخۡتِلَٰفُ أَلۡسِنَتِكُمۡ وَأَلۡوَٰنِكُمۡۚ\n(And the diversity of your tongues and colors), the tongue is in the mouth, which contains the diversity of languages, such as Arabic, Persian, Turkish, and Latin, while the diversity of images (colors) are white, black, and reddish. You can hardly see two identical people, and these differences are not caused by the sperm drop or the parents; rather, they are made by the only One Who is Allah, and this is a definite proof of the One Who controls all things and gives every creation its particular. Al-Qurtubi: 16/413.\nWhat does the diversity of tongues and colors indicate?\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ مَنَامُكُم بِٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱلنَّهَارِ وَٱبۡتِغَآؤُكُم مِّن فَضۡلِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَسۡمَعُونَ ٢٣\n(Seeking of His bounty), linking the (seeking) with the (bounty) indicates that the servant should not consider that obtaining his provision is due to his smartness; rather, he sees all that from his Lord's bounty. Al-Alusi: 11/33.\nWhat does linking the (seeking) with the (bounty) indicate in (Seeking of His bounty)?\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦ يُرِيكُمُ ٱلۡبَرۡقَ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعٗا وَيُنَزِّلُ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءٗ فَيُحۡيِۦ بِهِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَعۡدَ مَوۡتِهَآۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٤\nBenefiting from these signs is limited to those who understand, since a sound mind that is free of stubbornness and obstinacy, is sufficient for understanding the evidence and prudence in the mentioned signs. Ibn Ashur: 21/79.\nBenefiting from these signs is limited to those who understand. Why?\nwords\nمُحضَرُونَThey will remain\nتُظهِرُونَWhen you are at noon time\nلِلعَالِمِينَThose who have knowledge\nوَابتِغَاؤُكُم مِن فَضلِهِYour seeking of His bounty during the day\nخَوفًا وَطَمَعًاFear of thunderbolts, and hope for rain"],[407,"§Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nStart your prayer with this authentic supplication narrated in Sahih Muslim, \"I turn my face toward the One Who originated the heavens and earth, inclining to true faith, and I am not one of those who associate partners with Allah.\"\nPerform prayer in congregation with humbleness to attain a higher level of faith.\nSeek refuge with Allah, and warn those around you not to cause rifts among the believers in the community.\nguid\nThe universe around you is devotedly obedient and submissive to Allah, so do not be among those heedless deniers.\nAllah, the Almighty, often reveals in His Book that the cause for the rejection of those who turn away from Him is following their desires.\nDivision in religion is a habit of the polytheists, so, beware of emulating them.\nrefl\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يَبۡدَؤُاْ ٱلۡخَلۡقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيدُهُۥ وَهُوَ أَهۡوَنُ عَلَيۡهِۚ وَلَهُ ٱلۡمَثَلُ ٱلۡأَعۡلَىٰ فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلۡحَكِيمُ ٢٧\nAmong His sublime attributes are His Might and Wisdom, mentioned here, since the effects of these two attributes are manifest in beginning the creation and repeating it. Allah's Might entails His absolute self-sufficiency, therefore His absolute capability. His Wisdom entails His total knowledge. Ibn Ashur: 21/84.\nThese two attributes (All-Mighty, the All-Wise) are singled out for mention here. Why?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يَبۡدَؤُاْ ٱلۡخَلۡقَ ثُمَّ يُعِيدُهُۥ وَهُوَ أَهۡوَنُ عَلَيۡهِۚ\nMeaning: Repeating creation after they die will be (easier for him) than their original creation. This is as far as human minds are concerned. So, just as you affirm that He is able to originate creation, then, His ability to repeat it will be even easier. Al-Saadi: 640.\nResponses that employ logic are used in the Quran. Explain in light of this verse.\nكَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٨\nThe people who use reason refrain from obstinacy and turning away; and they seek the truth because of their sound intellect. Hence, the believers will have no doubts, and the heedless, who are misled by the misguidance of the polytheists, become believers due to these clear signs. This verse alludes to those who are stubborn in their shirk that they are not among the people who use reason nor will they benefit from these signs. Ibn Ashur: 21/87.\nWhat are the attributes of those who possess sound intellect?\nكَذَٰلِكَ نُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لِقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٢٨\nAs for those who do not understand, even if the revelations are explained to them and proof is presented to them, they have no sound minds with which to understand what is presented to them. It is the people of reason and understanding who should be addressed. Al-Saadi: 640.\nThe people of reason are addressed exclusively. Why?\nفَأَقِمۡ وَجۡهَكَ لِلدِّينِ حَنِيفٗاۚ فِطۡرَتَ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّتِي فَطَرَ ٱلنَّاسَ عَلَيۡهَاۚ لَا تَبۡدِيلَ لِخَلۡقِ ٱللَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلدِّينُ ٱلۡقَيِّمُ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣٠\nDefining Islam as the religion of Allah means the basis of its beliefs conforms to the natural disposition of mankind. The ordinances of Islam either coincide with human nature, as attested by sound mind, or do not contradict human nature. Ibn Ashur: 21/91.\nIslam is a religion that coincides with human natural disposition. What does that mean?\n۞مُنِيبِينَ إِلَيۡهِ وَٱتَّقُوهُ وَأَقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَلَا تَكُونُواْ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٣١ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ فَرَّقُواْ دِينَهُمۡ وَكَانُواْ شِيَعٗاۖ كُلُّ حِزۡبِۢ بِمَا لَدَيۡهِمۡ فَرِحُونَ ٣٢\nWhen Muslims differ with each other in religious issues due to independent reasoning, or disagreement over matters related to public interests, they must be cautious not to be divided into separate hostile sects. Ibn Ashur: 21/96.\nWhat should be the lesson learned by Muslims from the censure of the division of the People of the Book?\nمِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ فَرَّقُواْ دِينَهُمۡ وَكَانُواْ شِيَعٗاۖ كُلُّ حِزۡبِۢ بِمَا لَدَيۡهِمۡ فَرِحُونَ ٣٢\n(Sects), allied groups; each one allies with those who agree with its beliefs against others who do not, until they charged one another with infidelity, and went on to make their lives and wealth lawful for the taking. This was a definite sign that all of them were not on the right path. (Rejoicing), thinking that they were the only ones who knew the truth. Al-Biqai: 15/90-91.\nIn light of this verse, explain the risk of becoming divided over the religion of Allah.\nwords\nفِطرَةَ اللهِAdhere to the religion of Allah, (Islam)\nفَطَرَ النَّاسَ عَلَيهَاUpon which Allah has created mankind\nالقَيِّمِThe straight religion, leading to Allah\nفَرَّقُوا دِينَهُمThey changed their religion by believing in part of it and denying another part\nشِيَعًاDifferent sects and groups"],[408,"§Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nVisit or call one of your relatives to see how he is doing.\nGive charity to a poor person, or invite him to your home and serve him best.\nShare a message in which you explain the harms of usury or other social sins, etc.\nguid\nOnly the believers realize Allah's wisdom and arrangement of extending and restricting provisions.\nBe sincere in your giving, not every charity is acceptable.\nIf you see a calamity or disasters that have occurred, remember a sin that took place before it.\nrefl\nوَإِذَا مَسَّ ٱلنَّاسَ ضُرّٞ دَعَوۡاْ رَبَّهُم مُّنِيبِينَ إِلَيۡهِ ثُمَّ إِذَآ أَذَاقَهُم مِّنۡهُ رَحۡمَةً إِذَا فَرِيقٞ مِّنۡهُم بِرَبِّهِمۡ يُشۡرِكُونَ ٣٣\nMeaning: When these disbelievers are afflicted with disease or hardship, they call upon their Lord, which means that they cry out to Him to remove the hardship, Him alone without association to the idols since they know that no relief would ever come from them. Al-Qurtubi: 16/433.\nExplain how Allah censures those who remember Him during adversity, and forget Him during prosperity.\nوَإِذَآ أَذَقۡنَا ٱلنَّاسَ رَحۡمَةٗ فَرِحُواْ بِهَاۖ وَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ إِذَا هُمۡ يَقۡنَطُونَ ٣٦\nAllah says, (when) for mercy, and says, (if) for evil, to indicate that He often decrees more good to them than evil. Ibn Juzay: 2/169.\nHow can we infer from this verse that good things happen to people more often than evil?\nوَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ إِذَا هُمۡ يَقۡنَطُونَ ٣٦\nSince adversities result from committing sins, Allah alerts them to that fact, and refutes their despair while not backing away from their sins for which they are punished: (For what their hands have put forth). Al-Biqai: 15/95.\nList some of the effects of sins.\nوَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ إِذَا هُمۡ يَقۡنَطُونَ ٣٦\n(For what their hands have put forth), this is to point out that whatever afflicts them in worldly life is because of their deeds, which Allah made them a cause for painful effects that no one encompasses its subtleties except Allah. People have to reckon with themselves, evade the causes of these afflictions, and make up for what they had missed, for it will save them from evil and despair. This is a great etiquette of the revelation, where Allah says, (Whatever good happens to you is from Allah, but whatever bad happens to you is from yourself) [4:79]. Ibn Ashur: 21/101.\nWhat is the cause of calamities that strike mankind in this worldly life?\nوَمَآ ءَاتَيۡتُم مِّن رِّبٗا لِّيَرۡبُوَاْ فِيٓ أَمۡوَٰلِ ٱلنَّاسِ فَلَا يَرۡبُواْ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۖ وَمَآ ءَاتَيۡتُم مِّن زَكَوٰةٖ تُرِيدُونَ وَجۡهَ ٱللَّهِ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُضۡعِفُونَ ٣٩\nAl-Shaabi said: \"This verse means that whoever provides a service to another seeking worldly gain, this gain will never increase with Allah.\" Al-Qurtubi: 16/438.\nWill the servant be rewarded for helping another for worldly gains only?\nظَهَرَ ٱلۡفَسَادُ فِي ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِمَا كَسَبَتۡ أَيۡدِي ٱلنَّاسِ لِيُذِيقَهُم بَعۡضَ ٱلَّذِي عَمِلُواْ لَعَلَّهُمۡ يَرۡجِعُونَ ٤١\nGlory be to the One Who brings blessings through His trials and tests, and Who bestows grace through His punishment. Otherwise, if He caused them to taste the consequences of all that they have earned. He would not leave any living creature on the face of the earth. Al-Saadi: 643.\nThere is a blessing and bounty from Allah in trials. How?\nظَهَرَ ٱلۡفَسَادُ فِي ٱلۡبَرِّ وَٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِمَا كَسَبَتۡ أَيۡدِي ٱلنَّاسِ\nCorruption in land is by drought trials, and akin to it. Corruption at sea is by drowning, less fish to catch, and depression of trade, etc. All corruption is due to disbelief and disobedience by the people. Ibn Juzay: 2/169.\nWhat are the signs of the appearance of corruption and its causes?\nwords\nيَقنَطُونَThey despair of the end of affliction\nيَبسُطُHe extends\nوَيَقدِرُHe restricts\nرِبًاUsury\nلِيَربُوَTo gain more"],[409,"§Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nSend a message about the importance of righteousness to your collogues.\nWhen you see blowing winds or huge clouds, say what is mentioned in the Sunnah, \"O Allah, I ask you of its goodness, the goodness within it, and the goodness with which it has been sent; and I seek Your refuge with you from its harm, the harm within it, and the harm with which it has been sent.\"\nReflect on three of the effects of Allah's mercy on you and those around you, then give thanks to Him.\nguid\nThe requital befits the action.\nKnow that Allah's reward for the devotion of the believers is greater and larger than their deeds, as He rewards them with His bounty and vast mercy.\nDo not despair, for Allah's religion will prevail.\nrefl\nقُلۡ سِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ\nThe command to travel through the land includes both physical travel and mental or intellectual travel in the sense of pondering the fate of earlier nations. Al-Saadi: 643.\nIs travel through the land limited to physical movement?\nفَٱنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلُۚ كَانَ أَكۡثَرُهُم مُّشۡرِكِينَ ٤٢\nHence, beware of doing what they did, lest you meet the same fate, for the justice and wisdom of Allah are applicable at all times and places. Al-Saadi: 643.\nWhat is the benefit that one may gain by reflecting on the fate of those before him?\nقُلۡ سِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَٱنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلُۚ كَانَ أَكۡثَرُهُم مُّشۡرِكِينَ ٤٢\n(Most of them associated partners with Allah): This indicates that shirk alone was not the cause for destroying all, but rather most of them. Lesser sins than shirk caused the destruction of few of them. Moreover, this may indicate that their demise was due to the spread of shirk among them, where it became dominant. This signifies the risk of shirk and the fact that it is a trial that will not only befall the wrongdoers. Al-Alusi: 11/49.\nWhat are the causes for the destruction of nations? Which is the most serious one?\nإِنَّهُۥ لَا يُحِبُّ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ ٤٥\nYet, He is the Just with them who never transgresses.Ibn Kathir: 3/420.\nDoes disliking someone justify injustice?\nوَمِنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦٓ أَن يُرۡسِلَ ٱلرِّيَاحَ مُبَشِّرَٰتٖ وَلِيُذِيقَكُم مِّن رَّحۡمَتِهِۦ\nHe sends the rain to you to revive the land and people, and gives you a foretaste of His mercy so you know that it is His mercy that saves people and grants them provision, and thus you will be motivated to do more righteous deeds, by means of which the treasure of His mercy may be opened up for you. Al-Saadi: 643.\nHow does tasting Allah’s mercy influence the Muslims?\nوَلَقَدۡ أَرۡسَلۡنَا مِن قَبۡلِكَ رُسُلًا إِلَىٰ قَوۡمِهِمۡ فَجَآءُوهُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَٱنتَقَمۡنَا مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَجۡرَمُواْۖ وَكَانَ حَقًّا عَلَيۡنَا نَصۡرُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٤٧\n(And it is incumbent upon Us to help the believers), and save them from destruction. This gave glad tidings to the Prophet (ﷺ) of victory over the enemies. Alhasan said: \"He saved the believers with the Messengers from the destruction of nations.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/500.\nDoes the lengthy dominance of people of falsehood justify the believer’s despair? Explain in light of this verse.\nوَإِن كَانُواْ مِن قَبۡلِ أَن يُنَزَّلَ عَلَيۡهِم مِّن قَبۡلِهِۦ لَمُبۡلِسِينَ ٤٩ فَٱنظُرۡ إِلَىٰٓ ءَاثَٰرِ رَحۡمَتِ ٱللَّهِ كَيۡفَ يُحۡيِ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ بَعۡدَ مَوۡتِهَآۚ إِنَّ ذَٰلِكَ لَمُحۡيِ ٱلۡمَوۡتَىٰۖ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٞ ٥٠\nThis word: (Before), is repeated for confirmation, and to indicate the quickness of which people’s hearts can shift from despair to hope. Ibn Juzay: 2/170.\nThis word: (Before), is repeated twice in the same verse. Why?\nwords\nلاَّ مَرَدَّ لَهُIt cannot be averted\nيَصَّدَّعُونَPeople will be divided\nيَمهَدُونَThey prepare their places in Paradise\nفَتُثِيرُIt stirs up\nكِسَفًاFragments"],[410,"§Ar-Rum\ndeeds\nAsk Allah for the good end of life.\nRepent to Allah from all of your sins before the Day comes when repentance will not be of benefit .\nSupplicate Allah to purify your heart, and make it steadfast in His religion.\nguid\nBeware of wasting your youth and health in heedlessness and frivolity.\nKnowledge is a blessing from Allah, the Almighty, while effort and intelligence are just a cause, so say often, \"O Lord, increase my knowledge.\"\nThe worst state of man is when his heart is sealed because of his sins, and thus, he does not understand nor comprehend anything.\nrefl\n۞ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَكُم مِّن ضَعۡفٖ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ضَعۡفٖ قُوَّةٗ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ قُوَّةٖ ضَعۡفٗا وَشَيۡبَةٗۚ يَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٱلۡقَدِيرُ ٥٤\nAllah's attributes, knowledge and capability are mentioned here because progression [in creation] is a necessity of wisdom which relates to knowledge. Ibn Ashur: 21/128.\nThe verse ends with (the All-Knowing, the Most Capable). Why?\n۞ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَكُم مِّن ضَعۡفٖ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ ضَعۡفٖ قُوَّةٗ ثُمَّ جَعَلَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ قُوَّةٖ ضَعۡفٗا وَشَيۡبَةٗۚ يَخۡلُقُ مَا يَشَآءُۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡعَلِيمُ ٱلۡقَدِيرُ ٥٤\n(Created you in a state of weakness), the first weakness refers to the delicate liquid [man’s semen], and the frailness of childhood. The second and final weakness refers to old age. Ibn Juzay: 2/171.\nThere are two states of weaknesses in this verse. Explain.\nوَيَوۡمَ تَقُومُ ٱلسَّاعَةُ يُقۡسِمُ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُونَ مَا لَبِثُواْ غَيۡرَ سَاعَةٖۚ\nAllah reveals the ignorance of the disbelievers in this world and the Hereafter. In this world, they worship idols, and in the Hereafter, they will also display great ignorance. They will swear by Allah that they did not even stay for one hour in this world. They will intend to say that there was not enough time given to establish proof against them which would leave them with no excuse. Ibn Kathir: 3/424.\nThis verse indicates the disbelievers’ ignorance in worldly life and the Hereafter. Explain.\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡعِلۡمَ وَٱلۡإِيمَٰنَ لَقَدۡ لَبِثۡتُمۡ فِي كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ ٱلۡبَعۡثِۖ فَهَٰذَا يَوۡمُ ٱلۡبَعۡثِ وَلَٰكِنَّكُمۡ كُنتُمۡ لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٥٦\nCombining knowledge with faith to signify the importance of faith since knowledge without faith does not guide to the true beliefs that enable people to be saved in the Hereafter. Ibn Ashur: 21/131.\nThe verse combines knowledge with faith. Why?\nكَذَٰلِكَ يَطۡبَعُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٥٩\nMeaning: (Allah), the Almighty, the Most Capable, seals (the hearts of those who do not know), those who do not seek knowledge, or search for the truth; rather, they persist in believing fables, and inventing hoaxes, as compound ignorance prevents one from realizing the truth, and drives him to reject the rightful person. That is why it is said that compounded ignorance is worse than simple one. Al-Alusi: 11/60-61.\nExplain the risk of not seeking the truth and persisting in ignorance.\nفَٱصۡبِرۡ إِنَّ وَعۡدَ ٱللَّهِ حَقّٞۖ\nThis is something that should help one to be patient, for if he knows that his effort will not be wasted and that he will find it rewarded in full, then every hardship that he encounters will become insignificant, and it will become easier for him to bear every difficulty. Al-Saadi: 646.\nPatience is mentioned before stating that Allah's promise is true. Why?\nوَلَا يَسۡتَخِفَّنَّكَ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُوقِنُونَ ٦٠\nThis indicates that if a believer has a certain faith and a mature outlook, it will be easy for him to remain steadfast, but, for one who is weak in certainty, it indicates his immature outlook. Hence, the first example represents the core while the second represents the peels. Al-Saadi: 646.\nThis verse indicates the difference between the minds of those who are tested. Explain.\nwords\nمُصفَرًّاThe crops turned yellow due to corruption\nوَشَيبَةًOld age\nيُؤفَكُونَThey were deluded from the truth\nوَلاَ هُم يُستَعتَبُونَThey will not be asked to appease Allah\nوَلاَ يَستَخِفَّنَّكَLet them not disquiet you"],[411,"§Luqman\ndeeds\nPerform the five daily prayers in congregation from the opening Takbir.\nShare a message in which you explain the risk of singing, and that it leads away from the way of Allah.\nSeek refuge with Allah from behaving arrogantly toward the creation of Allah, or not submitting to the rules of Sharia.\nguid\nGuidance, mercy, and the attainment of the rank of benevolence are the fruits of following the Quran.\nWhoever listens to music, his heart will be distracted from the love of the Quran.\nUnlike arrogance, humility helps one to follow the truth.\nrefl\nتِلۡكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ ٱلۡحَكِيمِ ٢ هُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٗ لِّلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ ٣\nBut, although it is wise and precise, and it calls to every noble characteristic and forbids every ignoble characteristic, most people are deprived of being guided by it, and they turn away from believing in it and acting upon it, except those whom Allah guides and protects from misguidance. They are the ones who do good by worshiping their Lord, and showing kindness to others. Al-Saadi: 646.\nWhat are the positions of people toward this Book of wisdom?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ\nSingling out two good deeds for mention: Prayer which involves devotion, conversing with Allah and other actions of the heart, words and physical movements, and which helps them to do all kinds of good deeds; and zakah which purifies the giver of bad characteristics, benefits his Muslim brethren and meets his needs, and by means of it a person demonstrates clearly that he gives precedence to love of Allah over love of wealth, and that he gives away what he loves of wealth for the sake of that which is dearer to him, which is attaining the pleasure of Allah. Al-Saadi: 646.\nAmong all deeds, establishing prayer, and giving zakah are singled out. Why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَهُم بِٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ هُمۡ يُوقِنُونَ ٤\n(Those who establish prayer), they perform its essentials and options in a perfect way on a timely and consistent manner. Al-Biqai: 15/144.\nWhat does this expression, (Those who establish prayer) imply?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَشۡتَرِي لَهۡوَ ٱلۡحَدِيثِ لِيُضِلَّ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَيَتَّخِذَهَا هُزُوًاۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٦\nAbu Al-Sahba' Al-Bakri said: I asked Ibn Masoud (t) about the meaning of this verse, and he said: \"It means singing, by Allah, other than whom there is no god,\" and he repeated that three times. Ibrahim Al-Nakhai said: \"Singing is the seed of hypocrisy in the heart.\" Moreover, it is said: \"Singing is a call for shameful acts.\" Al-Baghawi: 3/506.\nIn light of this verse, explain the harms of singing based on the words of righteous predecessors.\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَشۡتَرِي لَهۡوَ ٱلۡحَدِيثِ لِيُضِلَّ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَيَتَّخِذَهَا هُزُوًاۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٦\n(Idle talk), whatever distracts people and wastes their time, like singing, comical things, and useless matters. All that can lead the soul from lust to animalistic traits and frivolous play like dancing, and akin to it, which takes him to the lowest of the low, while the one mentioned before him rose up through wisdom to the highest of high. Al-Biqai: 15/146.\nWhat is the risk of slipping into distractions?\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يَشۡتَرِي لَهۡوَ ٱلۡحَدِيثِ لِيُضِلَّ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَيَتَّخِذَهَا هُزُوًاۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٦\nQatadah said: \"By Allah, he may not spend money on it, but buying it means that he likes it, and the more misguided he is, the more he likes it, and the more he prefers falsehood to the truth and harmful things over beneficial things.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/426.\nDo those who are implied by this verse actually spend money to buy idle talk?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٞ مُّهِينٞ ٦\nJust as they showed no respect to the signs and path of Allah, so they will be humiliated in the painful, constant torment on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Kathir: 3/426.\nRecompensing those befits their action. Explain.\nwords\nهُزُوًاA mockery\nوَقرًاDeafness\nرَوَاسِيَFirm mountains\nأَن تَمِيدLest it shifts and moves\nوَبَثَّHe dispersed"],[412,"§Luqman\ndeeds\nToday, perform one of household chores that your mother does in order to know her virtue and patience.\nDuring prayer time, remind those whom you see sitting in the streets to pray.\nSpeak in a low voice and do not be loud and obnoxious.\nguid\nThere is no obedience to any created being if it involves disobedience to the Creator. This does not contravene kindness to parents, without committing a sin.\nFollow the way of those who turn to Allah in repentance among pious scholars.\nBeware of hidden sins.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَا لُقۡمَٰنَ ٱلۡحِكۡمَةَ أَنِ ٱشۡكُرۡ لِلَّهِۚ وَمَن يَشۡكُرۡ فَإِنَّمَا يَشۡكُرُ لِنَفۡسِهِۦۖ وَمَن كَفَرَ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَنِيٌّ حَمِيدٞ ١٢\nThe first thing of wisdom taught to Luqman was for his own good when Allah enjoined him to be grateful to Him for all the blessings he is beset with, among which is the blessing of being chosen by Allah. Ibn Ashur: 21/152.\nAccording to the verse, what was the first wisdom taught to Luqman (u)?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ لُقۡمَٰنُ لِٱبۡنِهِۦ وَهُوَ يَعِظُهُۥ يَٰبُنَيَّ لَا تُشۡرِكۡ بِٱللَّهِۖ إِنَّ ٱلشِّرۡكَ لَظُلۡمٌ عَظِيمٞ ١٣\nLuqman began his advice to his son by asking him not to associate partners with Allah, as the soul that pursues purity and perfection must first be cleared out of all bases of corruption and misguidance. Ibn Ashur: 21/155.\nLuqman (u) began by proscribing his son not to associate partners with Allah. Why?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ لُقۡمَٰنُ لِٱبۡنِهِۦ\nLuqman advised his son, the closest and most beloved of all people to him, who deserved to be given the best of his knowledge. Ibn Kathir: 3/428.\nGiving advice to one’s own son is significant. How?\nوَوَصَّيۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ بِوَٰلِدَيۡهِ حَمَلَتۡهُ أُمُّهُۥ وَهۡنًا عَلَىٰ وَهۡنٖ وَفِصَٰلُهُۥ فِي عَامَيۡنِ\nAllah mentions how the mother raises the child, and how she gets tired and suffers stress from staying up with the child night and day, to remind the son of her previous kind treatment of him. Ibn Kathir: 3/429.\nAllah mentions how the mother suffers in raising the child. Why?\nأَنِ ٱشۡكُرۡ لِي وَلِوَٰلِدَيۡكَ إِلَيَّ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ١٤\nIt is said that being grateful is to express gratitude to Allah for the blessing of belief, and express gratitude to the parents for the blessing of upbringing. Sufyan bin Uyaynah said: \"Whoever performs the five daily prayers, has expressed gratitude Allah, and whoever supplicates Allah for his parents at the end of prayers, has expressed gratitude his parents.\" Al-Qurtubi: 16/475.\nHow can someone be grateful to Allah and to his parents?\nوَأۡمُرۡ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَٱنۡهَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ وَٱصۡبِرۡ عَلَىٰ مَآ أَصَابَكَۖ\nLuqman knew that whoever enjoins what is good and forbids what is evil will inevitably encounter harm and annoyance from people, so he advised him to be patient. Ibn Kathir: 3/430.\nLuqman advised his son to be patient. Why?\nوَٱقۡصِدۡ فِي مَشۡيِكَ وَٱغۡضُضۡ مِن صَوۡتِكَۚ إِنَّ أَنكَرَ ٱلۡأَصۡوَٰتِ لَصَوۡتُ ٱلۡحَمِيرِ ١٩\nMeaning: Walk at a moderate pace, not haughtily nor fast. Ata’ said: Walk with dignity and calmness, as Allah says, (those who walk on earth humbly) [25:63]. Al-Baghawi: 3/511.\nHow does a person’s wisdom manifest in the way he walks?\nwords\nوَهنًاWeakness\nوَفِصَالُهُHis weaning\nأَنَابَTurned back in repentance\nحَبَّةٍ مِن خَردَلٍA mustard seed\nمِن عَزمِ الأُمُورِA matter of firm resolve to be pursued\nوَلاَ تُصَعِّر خَدَّكَDo not turn your face away in contempt\nمَرَحًاIn insolence"],[413,"§Luqman\ndeeds\nChoose a surah from the Quran and apply to it the three stages of seeking knowledge: A- Reflect upon its benefits. B- Study the surah with someone more knowledgeable than you. C- Read its interpretation from a book of interpretation.\nWrite down on a piece of paper some of the blessings you have, both apparent and hidden, to help you be grateful.\nShare a message in which you explain the risk of arguing without knowledge.\nguid\nBlind imitation and discarding reason is harmful.\nAdhering to religion is the lifeline and a safety valve.\nThe servant is tasked with delivering Allah's message, but the results are up to Him.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَوۡاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَخَّرَ لَكُم مَّا فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَأَسۡبَغَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ نِعَمَهُۥ ظَٰهِرَةٗ وَبَاطِنَةٗۗ\nHence, your job is to express gratitude for these blessings by loving the Bestower, submitting to Him and using them to help you obey Him, not using any of them to disobey Him. Al-Saadi: 649.\nHow should we be grateful to Allah for the blessings we have?\nوَأَسۡبَغَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ نِعَمَهُۥ ظَٰهِرَةٗ وَبَاطِنَةٗۗ\n(His favors, both apparent and hidden), the apparent favors are health, and wealth, etc. The hidden favors are things that no one knows about, among which is concealing evil deeds from others. Ibn Juzay: 2/174.\nGive examples of apparent and hidden favors.\nوَأَسۡبَغَ عَلَيۡكُمۡ نِعَمَهُۥ ظَٰهِرَةٗ وَبَاطِنَةٗۗ\nIbn Abbas (k) said: \"The apparent favor is Islam and the Quran, and the hidden favor is Allah's concealment of your sins, and His respite to you.\" Ad-Dahhak said: \"The apparent favor is the shaping and perfection of human form, and the hidden favor is knowledge.\" Al-Qurtubi: 3/512.\nMention two favors that you believe Allah selected you to have.\nوَمِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ مَن يُجَٰدِلُ فِي ٱللَّهِ بِغَيۡرِ عِلۡمٖ وَلَا هُدٗى وَلَا كِتَٰبٖ مُّنِيرٖ ٢٠\n(Without knowledge, guidance, or an enlightening scripture), this verse contains the stages of earning knowledge, which are: Independent reasoning, learning from a scholar, or reading the true scriptures. Ibn Ashur: 21/175.\nThis verse contains the three stages of earning knowledge. Explain.\n۞وَمَن يُسۡلِمۡ وَجۡهَهُۥٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ فَقَدِ ٱسۡتَمۡسَكَ بِٱلۡعُرۡوَةِ ٱلۡوُثۡقَىٰۗ وَإِلَى ٱللَّهِ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡأُمُورِ ٢٢\nMeaning: He devotes his worship sincerely to Allah, the Almighty. (And does good), since worshiping without doing good and submitting of the heart does not avail oneself. Al-Qurtubi: 16/487.\nHow do you submit your face to Allah? And why is it contingent on doing good?\n۞وَمَن يُسۡلِمۡ وَجۡهَهُۥٓ إِلَى ٱللَّهِ وَهُوَ مُحۡسِنٞ فَقَدِ ٱسۡتَمۡسَكَ بِٱلۡعُرۡوَةِ ٱلۡوُثۡقَىٰۗ وَإِلَى ٱللَّهِ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلۡأُمُورِ ٢٢\n(Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing of what is in the hearts), since part of the disbelief of the polytheists is apparent while another is hidden. Ibn Ashur: 21/178.\nThe verse ends with (Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing of what is in the hearts). Why?\nوَلَوۡ أَنَّمَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ مِن شَجَرَةٍ أَقۡلَٰمٞ وَٱلۡبَحۡرُ يَمُدُّهُۥ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِۦ سَبۡعَةُ أَبۡحُرٖ مَّا نَفِدَتۡ كَلِمَٰتُ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٢٧\nThis verse points to the abundance of Allah's Words, which means His knowledge. It means that if all the trees on earth were pens and the sea were ink, replenished constantly by seven more seas, and these pens wrote the Words of Allah, the trees and seas would have been exhausted, because they are finite, but the Words of Allah would not because they are infinite. Ibn Juzay: 2/175.\nMention the lesson learned from this verse.\nwords\nسَخَّرَ لَكُمHe made subject to you\nوَأَسبَغَHe amply bestowed upon you\nبِالعُروَةِ الوُثقَىThe firmest cause to Allah\nعَاقِبَةُOutcome, return\nغَلِيظٍMassive, horrible"],[414,"§Luqman\ndeeds\nSee pictures of ships, or read about them to get a sense of Allah's great blessing upon us through them.\nRecall a difficult situation from which Allah Has saved you, and thank Him for His deliverance, and then do a righteous deed in gratitude to Allah.\nRecall something of the world's adornments that your heart is attached to, then list three of its flaws to lessen your attachment to it.\nguid\nSome of today's polytheists are worse than those of Quraysh, since they associate partners with Allah in prosperity and adversity, while the polytheists of Quraysh used to associate partners with Allah in prosperity, but become sincere to Him in times of adversity.\nClaiming to know the unseen is blasphemy, and whoever claims that any of the Prophets and allies of Allah knew the unseen, has claimed the association of a created being with the Creator.\nBeware of procrastination, and hasten to work.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ يُولِجُ ٱلَّيۡلَ فِي ٱلنَّهَارِ وَيُولِجُ ٱلنَّهَارَ فِي ٱلَّيۡلِ وَسَخَّرَ ٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَۖ كُلّٞ يَجۡرِيٓ إِلَىٰٓ أَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗى وَأَنَّ ٱللَّهَ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ خَبِيرٞ ٢٩\nIn this verse, the mention of the night comes first because it is more wondrous in the sense that its darkness covers all the daylight. Ibn Ashur: 21/185.\nIn this verse, the mention of the night comes first. Why?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱلۡفُلۡكَ تَجۡرِي فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِنِعۡمَتِ ٱللَّهِ لِيُرِيَكُم مِّنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٖ ٣١\nThe reason for singling out patience and gratitude for mention among the qualities of faith is because they are more relevant to the situation of traveling by sea, where a traveler is subjected to both danger and safety, which call for patience and gratitude. Ibn Ashur: 21/190.\nTraits of patience and gratitude are singled out for mention when traveling by sea. Why?\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٖ ٣١\nMeaning: Everyone who is patient with Allah’s decree, and grateful for His blessing. Those who focus on the meanings of words said: This description applies to every believer, since patience and gratitude are the best among the qualities of faith. Al-Qurtubi: 16/493.\nThe verse ends with the mention of these two great qualities. Why?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱلۡفُلۡكَ تَجۡرِي فِي ٱلۡبَحۡرِ بِنِعۡمَتِ ٱللَّهِ لِيُرِيَكُم مِّنۡ ءَايَٰتِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٖ ٣١\nIn the original Arabic text, the words (patient and grateful) are expressed in emphasized forms to indicate that those who revere Allah in prosperity as well as in adversity are only those whom Allah instilled such qualities into their nature, and helped them keep their covenant and refrain from disloyalty, in conforming with the sound natural disposition, and how few they are. Al-Biqai: 15/206.\n(Patient and grateful) are expressed in emphasized form. Why?\nوَإِذَا غَشِيَهُم مَّوۡجٞ كَٱلظُّلَلِ دَعَوُاْ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِصِينَ لَهُ ٱلدِّينَ فَلَمَّا نَجَّىٰهُمۡ إِلَى ٱلۡبَرِّ فَمِنۡهُم مُّقۡتَصِدٞۚ وَمَا يَجۡحَدُ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَآ إِلَّا كُلُّ خَتَّارٖ كَفُورٖ ٣٢\n(Treacherous), a traitor who denies Allah's favor by his disloyalty. Ibn Juzay: 2/176.\nThe disbeliever is a traitor. Why?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ ٱتَّقُواْ رَبَّكُمۡ وَٱخۡشَوۡاْ يَوۡمٗا لَّا يَجۡزِي وَالِدٌ عَن وَلَدِهِۦ وَلَا مَوۡلُودٌ هُوَ جَازٍ عَن وَالِدِهِۦ شَيۡـًٔاۚ\nAllah instructs people to fear Him, which means complying with His commands and refraining from what He forbids. He also reminds them to fear the Day of Resurrection, that difficult day when no one will care for anyone except himself, and (no father will avail his son, nor will a son avail his father anything). No one will be able to increase his good deeds or decrease his bad deeds; everyone’s deeds will have been decided and the requital for those deeds will become due. Allah draws our attention to this momentous day so as to give the individual strength and make it easier for him to fear Allah. Al-Saadi: 652.\nAllah often mentions in the Quran the horrors of the Day of Resurrection. Why?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عِندَهُۥ عِلۡمُ ٱلسَّاعَةِ وَيُنَزِّلُ ٱلۡغَيۡثَ وَيَعۡلَمُ مَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡحَامِۖ وَمَا تَدۡرِي نَفۡسٞ مَّاذَا تَكۡسِبُ غَدٗاۖ وَمَا تَدۡرِي نَفۡسُۢ بِأَيِّ أَرۡضٖ تَمُوتُۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ خَبِيرُۢ ٣٤\nIn the words of the Prophet (ﷺ), these five knowledge areas are called \"The keys of the unseen,\" with which he interpreted this verse, (He alone has the keys of the unseen; no one knows them except Him) [6:59]. In Sahih Al-Bukhari, Ibn Omar (t) narrated that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"The keys of the unseen are five\", then he recited: (Indeed, Allah has the knowledge of the Hour). Ibn Ashur: 21/198.\nThis verse mentions five knowledge areas. What are they called?\nwords\nيُولِجُEntering; by reducing the night hours so the day becomes longer, and the opposite is true\nغَشِيَهُمComes over them\nكَالظُّلَلِLike clouds, or shady mountains\nخَتَّارٍA treacherous who breaks the covenant"],[415,"§As-Sajdah\ndeeds\nRemind the Imam of your mosque to read Surat As-Sajdah and Surat Al-Insan in Fajr prayer on Fridays, because it is a Sunnah.\nSupplicate Allah, the Almighty, to manage your affairs, and give you knowledge that is of benefit, for He is the One Who manages, and the All-Knowing.\nSupplicate Allah to perfect your moral character as He perfected your creation.\nguid\nThis verse shows the greatness of Allah's ability in managing all affairs.\nHearing and sight are two blessings, and showing gratitude for them is by using them for what brings us closer to Allah.\nReflect on the moment of death when you will meet Allah, the Almighty, with your deeds, whether good or bad.\nrefl\nالٓمٓ ١ تَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهِ مِن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢\nAbu Hurairah said, \"The Prophet (ﷺ) used to recite in Fajr on Fridays: (Alif Lam Meem ` [This is] the revelation of...), As-Sajdah, and (Has there [not] come upon man...).\" Ibn Kathir: 6/358.\nReflect on Surat As-Sajdah, then try to find the wisdom of reciting it in Fajr prayer on Fridays.\nتَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهِ مِن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢\nAllah states that this noble Book has been sent down from the Lord of the worlds, Who cares for them and showers them with His blessings. One of the greatest means through which Allah educated, cared for and guided people is this Book, in which is all that could put their affairs straight and perfect their manners. Al-Saadi: 653.\nWhat is meant by the Lordship description in (Lord of the worlds)?\nتَنزِيلُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ لَا رَيۡبَ فِيهِ مِن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ ٢\nThis Surah begins by praising the Quran, as it is the cumulation of guidance of which this and all Surahs contain. Since the rejection of this Quran is the cumulation of misguidance of the misguided, Allah has made the Quran a guidance for mankind, and He selected the Arabs for the honor of being the first to receive this Book. Ibn Ashur: 21/205.\nThe verse praises the Holy Quran. Explain.\nٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَمَا بَيۡنَهُمَا فِي سِتَّةِ أَيَّامٖ ثُمَّ ٱسۡتَوَىٰ عَلَى ٱلۡعَرۡشِۖ مَا لَكُم مِّن دُونِهِۦ مِن وَلِيّٖ وَلَا شَفِيعٍۚ أَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٤\nMeaning: You do not listen to these admonishments, hence you do not take heed; or you listen to them, but you do not take heed. In the first case, the censure is for both, not listening and not taking heed. In the second case, the censure is for not taking heed despite listening. Al-Alusi: 11/118.\nWhen does one benefit from listening to an admonishment?\nمَا لَكُم مِّن دُونِهِۦ مِن وَلِيّٖ وَلَا شَفِيعٍۚ أَفَلَا تَتَذَكَّرُونَ ٤\nMeaning: O mankind, you do not have an ally who can protect you against Allah if He intends to harm you, nor an intercessor who can intercede with Him for you if He punishes you for disobeying Him. So, take Him as an ally, and seek help with your affairs through His obedience, as He will protect you against anyone who intends to harm you, but no one can ward off what He intends, because no one can vanquish Him. Al-Tabari: 20/166.\nThe heart and body should be attached only to Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nيُدَبِّرُ ٱلۡأَمۡرَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ إِلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِ ثُمَّ يَعۡرُجُ إِلَيۡهِ فِي يَوۡمٖ كَانَ مِقۡدَارُهُۥٓ أَلۡفَ سَنَةٖ مِّمَّا تَعُدُّونَ ٥\nThis indicates that people's plans of matters are useless against Allah's management. A blissful servant is one who forgoes his planning, and become content with Allah’s management of matters. Al-Alusi: 11/138.\nWhat is the benefit of reliance upon Allah?\nذَٰلِكَ عَٰلِمُ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِ ٱلۡعَزِيزُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٦\nThese attributes of Allah, (The All-Mighty, the Most Merciful), come after mentioning that He created the creation by His capability without help, hence, His attribute, the All Mighty -which means Self-Sufficient- is manifested. Moreover, He created them in graceful conditions, hence He is the Most Merciful to them, as He made their living suitable for them, providing them with good, and protecting them from evil. Ibn Ashur: 21 /215.\nThis verse ends with these attributes of Allah, (The All-Mighty, the Most Merciful). Why?\nwords\nافتَرَاهُHe invented it\nاستَوَىHe rose in a manner that suits His Majesty\nيَعرُجُ إِلَيهِIt ascends to Him\nنَسلَهُHis offspring\nسُلاَلَةٍA sperm-drop extracted from the whole body\nمَهِينٍDelicate, frail\nضَلَلنَا فِي الأَرضِWe became dust after death"],[416,"§As-Sajdah\ndeeds\nPerform the prostration of recitation when you read this verse.\nSet your alarm to get up and pray at night and supplicate your Lord.\nGive to charity.\nguid\nDo good deeds before you wish you can do them, but will not be able to.\nGuidance is at the Hand of Allah, so ask Him for it.\nConceal a righteous deed of yours, so that only Allah knows about it.\nrefl\nوَلَوۡ تَرَىٰٓ إِذِ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُونَ نَاكِسُواْ رُءُوسِهِمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ رَبَّنَآ أَبۡصَرۡنَا وَسَمِعۡنَا فَٱرۡجِعۡنَا نَعۡمَلۡ صَٰلِحًا إِنَّا مُوقِنُونَ ١٢\nMeaning: If only you could see the state of the criminals on the Day of Resurrection, you would see a horrible sight. (Lowering their heads): An indication of humiliation, distress, and regret. (Our Lord, we have now seen and heard), our Lord, we now know the truth. Ibn Juzay: 2/178.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the criminals will lower their heads. Why?\nإِنَّمَا يُؤۡمِنُ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا ذُكِّرُواْ بِهَا خَرُّواْۤ سُجَّدٗاۤ وَسَبَّحُواْ بِحَمۡدِ رَبِّهِمۡ وَهُمۡ لَا يَسۡتَكۡبِرُونَ۩ ١٥\nMeaning: They fall in prostration on their faces in honor of His verses, and in fear of His power and punishment. Al-Qurtubi: 17/27.\nHow should the Muslim react when reminded of Allah’s verses?\nتَتَجَافَىٰ جُنُوبُهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡمَضَاجِعِ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُمۡ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعٗا وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ١٦\n(Their sides forsake their beds), their sides arise from their beds; they abandon their beds at night due to their frequent voluntary prayers, and whoever performed Isha and Fajr prayers in congregation, has done his part of that. Ibn Juzay: 2/179.\nWhat motivates the believers to abandon their beds?\nتَتَجَافَىٰ جُنُوبُهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡمَضَاجِعِ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُمۡ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعٗا وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ١٦\n(And aspiration), they aspire to Allah's pleasure that entails His reward. The word (aspiration) is used instead of “hope” to indicate their awareness of their shortcomings, and the fact that they do not think much of their good deeds. Rather, they aspire to receive Allah's bounty without relying on them. Even though they seek Allah’s mercy without a cause, they become more hopeful with a cause, as they never despair of His mercy. Al-Biqai: 15/256.\nThe word (aspiration) is used instead of \"hope\", why?\nتَتَجَافَىٰ جُنُوبُهُمۡ عَنِ ٱلۡمَضَاجِعِ يَدۡعُونَ رَبَّهُمۡ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعٗا وَمِمَّا رَزَقۡنَٰهُمۡ يُنفِقُونَ ١٦\n(And spend out of what We have provided for them), when mentioning that they give preference to being closer to Allah over their physical enjoyment, He mentions their same preference when it comes to another enjoyment, which is wealth. Ibn Ashur: 21/229.\nThis part of the verse: (And spend out of what We have provided for them) comes after mentioning nighttime prayer. Why?\nفَلَا تَعۡلَمُ نَفۡسٞ مَّآ أُخۡفِيَ لَهُم مِّن قُرَّةِ أَعۡيُنٖ\nMeaning: No one knows the vastness of what Allah has concealed for them of everlasting joy in Paradise and delights such as no one has ever seen. Because they concealed their good deeds, Allah concealed the reward for them, a befitting recompense that suits their deeds. Al-Hasan Al-Basri said, \"Those people concealed their good deeds, hence, Allah concealed for them what no eye has seen and what has never crossed the mind of man.\" Ibn Kathir: 3/443.\nAllah has concealed much of the reward of the people who will be in Paradise. Why?\nكُلَّمَآ أَرَادُوٓاْ أَن يَخۡرُجُواْ مِنۡهَآ أُعِيدُواْ فِيهَا\nEvery time they want to emerge from it, because the pain has reached such a high degree, they will be driven back into it. Hence, they will lose any hope of relief and will become extremely distressed. Al-Saadi: 656.\nThis part of the verse indicates the intensity of their punishment. How?\nwords\nنَاكِسُوا رُؤُوسِهِمLowering their heads in disgrace\nحَقَّ القَولُMy Word will be fulfilled\nالجِنَّةِJinn being\nتَتَجَافَىTheir sides part and arise\nالمَضَاجِعِSleeping beds\nمَا أُخفِيَ لَهُمWhat has been hidden for them as a reward\nمِن قُرَّةِ أَعيُنٍJoy and Delight\nالمَأوَىPlace of residence\nنُزُلًاAccommodation"]])